<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Okitanawate</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1584</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Okitanawate was fought in 1584 near Shimabara in Hizen province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ryuzoji-takanobu">Ryuzoji Takanobu</a> attacked Arima Harunobu, who was supported by a Shimazu army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimazu-iehisa">Shimazu Iehisa</a>; Takanobu was killed and his army routed. The defeat broke Ryuzoji power and left the Shimazu the leading force in Kyushu until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a>'s invasion of 1587.</p></div>
